To view or inspect the contents inside the Bitget Wallet.apk file directly from your Ubuntu terminal, you can choose one of the following methods depending on what you want to see:
## Method 1: View the Inner Files & Assets (Like a Zip file)
An APK is just a compressed ZIP archive. You can list every image, layout, and code file inside it using the unzip tool without extracting it:

unzip -l "Bitget Wallet.apk"

(If you want to view it using a graphical interface, you can just right-click the file in your Ubuntu folder manager and choose "Open with Archive Manager").
## Method 2: View App Information (Package name, Version, Permissions)
To read the compiled Android manifest file and view technical details like version numbers, app names, and required hardware permissions, use aapt2:

aapt2 dump badging "Bitget Wallet.apk"

(If aapt2 is missing, you can install it quickly by running sudo apt install aapt2).
## Method 3: Decompile the App to View Source Code
If you want to view the actual readable application source code, resources, and XML layouts, you can use jadx or apktool:

# Decompile using apktool to view layouts and resources
sudo apt install apktool
apktool d "Bitget Wallet.apk"

This will create a new readable folder containing the app's components.
